# /etc/deltav/deltav.env: settings for the Delta-V daemon (deltav.service).
# Keep this file readable by root only (chmod 600): it holds the API token.
# Every "deltav serve" flag has a variable; "deltav serve --help" lists them.

# Where Envoys connect (xDS and telemetry). The client hosts must reach it.
#DELTAV_GRPC_ADDR=0.0.0.0:18000

# The HTTP API, web UI and /metrics. Loopback by default, which needs no
# token; reach the web UI through an SSH tunnel:
#   ssh -L 18080:127.0.0.1:18080 <this host>
# To serve it on the network instead, bind another address and set a long
# random token. systemd reads this file literally: it runs no commands and
# expands no $(...). Generate the token in a shell and paste its output:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# The daemon speaks plain HTTP, so the token crosses the network in clear:
# put a TLS reverse proxy or an SSH tunnel in front of any address other
# than loopback.
#DELTAV_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1:18080
#DELTAV_API_TOKEN=

# How often each attached VAST cluster is read (three GETs).
#DELTAV_VAST_POLL_INTERVAL=10s
